# Royal Potter — palette

Eight colours drawn from [key-art.png](key-art.png). Samples refer to the final
1080×1920 image, with coordinates measured from its top-left corner. Use these as
base colours; lighting supplies the two or three shade bands.

| Colour | Hex | Use in the artwork | Sample (x, y) |
|---|---|---|---|
| Potter's Ink | `#2A2420` | Warm dark outlines and deep creases | Locked brief colour; nearest image pixel is `#2A2421` |
| Wet Terracotta | `#AD5C37` | Unfired tower and clay slip | 496, 1248 |
| Cream Plaster | `#F0D6AE` | Ceramic walls, tower lips and pale glaze | 691, 304 |
| Warm Oak | `#9F683B` | Wheel surround and workshop timber | 200, 1716 |
| Courtyard Sage | `#959B68` | Green glazed watchtower | 421, 624 |
| Storybook Sky | `#7BA2DA` | Open blue sky above the castle | 540, 67 |
| Kiln Gold | `#F2B345` | Warm glow inside the kiln | 102, 876 |
| Royal Rose | `#B2675D` | Castle's dusty rose banner | 670, 624 |

## Six player glaze colours

These reuse the scene palette so any combination belongs in the same castle.
Their names are the proposed English labels for the glaze picker.

| Glaze | Hex | Character |
|---|---|---|
| Cream Crown | `#F0D6AE` | Warm ivory, like the castle walls |
| Sage Keep | `#959B68` | Gentle green, like the round watchtower |
| Sky Spire | `#7BA2DA` | Clear blue, echoing the sky and blue dome |
| Honey Hall | `#F2B345` | Golden yellow, used sparingly for warmth |
| Rose Turret | `#B2675D` | Muted rose, echoing the royal banners |
| Terracotta Throne | `#AD5C37` | Earthy red-brown with a fired gloss |

Wet clay always starts as Wet Terracotta. Even when the player chooses Terracotta
Throne, firing changes its broad wet sheen into small, crisp glaze highlights.
Keep highlights cream-tinted and preserve visible throwing rings beneath every glaze.
